WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:05.109
Packed with a cast of young '80s stars, Joel
Schumacher's The Lost Boys all but founded

00:00:05.109 --> 00:00:07.260
the idea that vampires could be sexy.

00:00:07.420 --> 00:00:11.719
While not without its fair share of cheese,
The Lost Boys has aged pretty well — but

00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:12.640
what about the cast?

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:14.700
"Bottoms up, man.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:16.000
Woo!"

00:00:16.060 --> 00:00:20.880
While stars Cory Haim, Edward Hermann, Brooke
McCarter, and Bernard Hughes have sadly passed

00:00:20.890 --> 00:00:25.010
away since its release, Lost Boys boasts a
huge cast to catch up with.

00:00:25.010 --> 00:00:28.520
Here's what The Lost Boys stars have been
up to over the past few decades.

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:30.480
Kiefer Sutherland

00:00:30.860 --> 00:00:35.380
Of all the Lost Boys, Kiefer Sutherland has
maintained his household name status the best,

00:00:35.390 --> 00:00:39.660
even if people don't know that his full name
is actually Kiefer William Frederick Dempsey

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:41.300
George Rufus Sutherland.

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:42.400
That was a mouthful…

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:43.540
"Fun, huh?"

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:48.360
He'd previously starred in Stand By Me, but
it was his role as David the vampire that

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:50.700
first secured Sutherland's future status in
Hollywood.

00:00:50.840 --> 00:00:55.600
He quickly went on to appear in a slew of
major motion pictures, including Young Guns,

00:00:55.780 --> 00:00:57.579
Flatliners, and A Time to Kill.

00:00:57.580 --> 00:01:01.100
He also starred as the lead in the mega hit
TV series 24.

00:01:01.180 --> 00:01:05.640
Most recently, Sutherland returned to the
small screen for a similar drama series called

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:09.040
Designated Survivor and will even appear in
the Flatliners reboot.

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:10.820
Corey Feldman

00:01:11.320 --> 00:01:13.860
In some ways, Corey Feldman never had a childhood.

00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:18.680
Known for his roles in Gremlins, The Goonies,
Stand by Me, and The 'Burbs, Feldman — like

00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:23.540
his Lost Boys co-star and real-life friend
Corey Haim — endured tumultuous early years.

00:01:23.760 --> 00:01:28.670
He told the Chicago Tribune, "Most people
in society are all given equal rights to decide

00:01:28.670 --> 00:01:29.889
what their future should be.

00:01:29.889 --> 00:01:31.420
I never had that opportunity."

00:01:31.420 --> 00:01:35.120
That's been reflected in the tabloid reports
that have dogged Feldman as an adult.

00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:40.920
In 2013, Vice published a now-infamous firsthand
account of a shindig at his crib, dubbed "The

00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:45.940
Feldmansion," describing a raucous affair
where scantily clad women wearing only lingerie

00:01:45.940 --> 00:01:50.640
attend for free, while men can pay for entry
and "private angel service," whatever that

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:51.140
entails.

00:01:51.320 --> 00:01:55.740
He also headlines a zany musical stage act
called Corey's Angels and has bitten back

00:01:55.740 --> 00:01:58.360
at criticisms of his new professional adventure.

00:01:58.500 --> 00:02:01.680
"A lot of people get hate in the beginning
because we're doing something new - never

00:02:01.689 --> 00:02:02.770
been done before.

00:02:02.770 --> 00:02:06.760
It's all about innovation and being artists
We can't be afraid to show our art."

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:08.460
Jason Patric

00:02:09.080 --> 00:02:13.500
In his breakout role, Jasic Patric played
Michael, the handsome protagonist who gives

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:18.019
into peer pressure, chugs some vampire blood,
and becomes a sunglasses-wearing blood-sucker

00:02:18.020 --> 00:02:19.140
who sleeps all day.

00:02:19.240 --> 00:02:23.400
After defeating his real-life friend Kiefer
Sutherland on the big screen — and stealing

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:28.080
his real-life fiancée Julia Roberts — Patric
went on to nab some other memorable roles.

00:02:28.269 --> 00:02:33.540
He played Jim Raynor in Rush, Shakes in Sleepers,
Officer Alex Shaw in Speed 2: Cruise Control,

00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:36.880
and Dr. Theo Yedlin in Wayward Pines, to name
a few.

00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:41.220
But Patric's most recent time in the media
spotlight has been pretty unrelated to his

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:41.720
career.

00:02:41.780 --> 00:02:46.640
He fought a heated custody battle with ex-girlfriend
Danielle Schreiber after donating his sperm

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:50.140
to her and fighting for his parental rights
to the resulting child.

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:54.300
Shared custody was ultimately ordered for
the kid in question, but not before Schreiber

00:02:54.310 --> 00:02:59.220
accused Patric of having been physically and
verbally abusive to her and prompting another

00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:00.820
legal spectacle between them.

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:04.799
For what it's worth, Patric still remembers
his time on The Lost Boys fondly.

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:08.500
"It's just nice that all these years later
I'm still very good friends with Jamie Gertz,

00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:11.660
very good friends with Kiefer, and it was
a special time."

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:13.520
Dianne Wiest

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:18.080
Before landing the role of Lucy in The Lost
Boys, Dianne Wiest was already fairly well

00:03:18.090 --> 00:03:22.540
known for her roles as Vi Moore in Footloose,
Holly in Hannah and Her Sisters, and Bea in

00:03:22.540 --> 00:03:23.400
Radio Days.

00:03:23.540 --> 00:03:27.420
But afterwards, she continued to accelerate
her character actress status by appearing

00:03:27.420 --> 00:03:32.780
in Bullets Over Broadway, Ron Howard's Parenthood,
Edward Scissorhands, I Am Sam, and more.

00:03:32.970 --> 00:03:37.180
Despite having an extensive list of credits
and pair of Academy Awards for Best Supporting

00:03:37.189 --> 00:03:41.670
Actress in her trophy cabinet, Wiest claims
her career has been hampered by being typecast

00:03:41.670 --> 00:03:44.320
in the type of mother role we see her play
in The Lost Boys.

00:03:44.500 --> 00:03:48.360
She told the New York Times that the only
offers she ever gets is to play "a nice mom

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:49.020
and that's it."

00:03:49.400 --> 00:03:50.910
"Has everyone gone crazy here?

00:03:50.910 --> 00:03:52.680
What's the matter with all of you?"

00:03:52.840 --> 00:03:56.880
Indeed, her current starring role features
her as just that in the small screen series

00:03:56.880 --> 00:03:57.980
Life in Pieces.

00:03:58.720 --> 00:03:59.840
Jami Gertz

00:04:00.260 --> 00:04:04.560
Before appearing in The Lost Boys, Jami Gertz
had already starred in The Facts of Life and

00:04:04.569 --> 00:04:05.680
Sixteen Candles.

00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:09.360
However, Gertz's career really took off after
playing Star in The Lost Boys.

00:04:09.460 --> 00:04:14.760
She immediately went on to play Monica Tomanski
in Listen to Me, Toby in Jersey Girl, and

00:04:14.760 --> 00:04:17.360
Lily Ruscio in the television series Sibs.

00:04:17.480 --> 00:04:21.600
She also appeared as Dr. Melissa Reeves in
the blockbuster tornado drama Twister before

00:04:21.780 --> 00:04:27.080
landing the recurring roles of Dr. Nina Pomerantz
in ER and Kimmy Bishop in Ally McBeal.

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:31.320
Most recently, Gertz starred in the small
screen series The Neighbors, along with other

00:04:31.320 --> 00:04:32.340
network cameos.

00:04:32.720 --> 00:04:34.040
Jamison Newlander

00:04:34.460 --> 00:04:38.200
Not every Lost Boys star has been able to
break out of the film's shell.

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:42.760
Jamison Newlander is still known for his role
as Alan Frog in the film and doesn't boast

00:04:42.760 --> 00:04:45.440
as much star power as some of his former co-stars.

00:04:45.590 --> 00:04:49.660
He told Collider, "People don't necessarily
recognize me right away 'cause I look a little

00:04:49.660 --> 00:04:50.160
different.

00:04:50.220 --> 00:04:54.020
when they realize that I'm a Frog brother
and I was in The Lost Boys, it's exciting."

00:04:54.280 --> 00:04:58.480
In addition to playing the less famous Frog
brother in the first film, Newlander also

00:04:58.480 --> 00:05:00.130
reprised his role for the sequels.

00:05:00.130 --> 00:05:05.840
"Back when Joel and Corey and I got together
and we were like coming up with these characters

00:05:05.840 --> 00:05:07.130
you know something about it really worked.

00:05:07.130 --> 00:05:07.820
"it spoke to people."

00:05:08.680 --> 00:05:09.540
Billy Wirth

00:05:09.920 --> 00:05:14.520
After playing the tall scary vampire who takes
an arrow to the chest and gets fried by a

00:05:14.530 --> 00:05:18.310
stereo, Billy Wirth has kept himself busy,
even if he never quite reached the marquee

00:05:18.310 --> 00:05:20.210
status of his other fanged friends.

00:05:20.210 --> 00:05:24.650
He appeared in a list of films that includes
Body Snatchers and Boys on the Side, while

00:05:24.650 --> 00:05:27.520
also making appearances on shows like Sex
and the City.

00:05:28.280 --> 00:05:29.240
Alex Winter

00:05:29.820 --> 00:05:33.920
After playing Marko in The Lost Boys, Alex
Winter went on to play another of the most

00:05:33.920 --> 00:05:38.700
iconic roles of the '80s as one-half of the
title pair in Bill &amp; Ted's Excellent Adventure

00:05:38.700 --> 00:05:39.200
movies.

00:05:39.200 --> 00:05:43.040
Though he's done a few other things as well,
he'll probably always be best known for that

00:05:43.040 --> 00:05:43.540
role.

00:05:43.540 --> 00:05:45.260
And Winter doesn't mind it much.

00:05:45.260 --> 00:05:49.500
In fact, even he is not ready to retire his
goofy time-travelling adventure series just

00:05:49.500 --> 00:05:50.000
yet.

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:53.740
He told The Next Web that the third installment
of Bill and Ted's excellent adventures is

00:05:53.750 --> 00:05:57.340
coming soon, saying, "The fun thing about
them is that they're ageless.

00:05:57.340 --> 00:05:59.680
You play them in terms of who they are spiritually.

00:05:59.680 --> 00:06:02.150
Their mannerism and physicality are not tied
to age.

00:06:02.150 --> 00:06:04.050
We played them like 9-year-old kids.

00:06:04.050 --> 00:06:05.740
… It will be funnier because they're older."

00:06:05.940 --> 00:06:07.080
"No way."

00:06:08.280 --> 00:06:09.020
"Yes way."

00:06:09.220 --> 00:06:10.060
Thanks for watching!

00:06:10.260 --> 00:06:12.760
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:06:12.900 --> 00:06:15.120
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

